{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788120585668,"sessionID":"ses_fabb535ccffe1uMPqoZsBbW0jp","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"chatcmpl-tool-a96a69f5d9b63b05","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"just --list"},"output":"Available recipes:\n    check          # The fast inner loop: skips the docs mega-test, the suite's ~137s long pole. Gate on `just test`.\n    checks         # The repo's mechanical checks, the same surface the Stop hook runs.\n    clippy         # Run clippy with the repo's lint set, the same surface the Stop hook checks.\n    default        # List available recipes.\n    drive          # The autonomous drive loop: a tick every 600s, live colorized output, Ctrl-C to stop. Run ONE.\n    euler-data DIR # `just test`. DIR holds your own copies of the raw data texts; fails loudly, never skips.\n    fmt            # Formatter check over every .toy file from the repo root down (exit 1 on drift).\n    fmt-write      # Rewrite drifted files in place (same exit code as the check).\n    peek           # Watch the current coordinator tick live (detaches with Ctrl-C, tick untouched).\n    test           # The final gate: the full test suite. Landing requires this green.\n    tick           # Fire one coordinator tick right now (zero tokens if there is nothing to do).\n","metadata":{"output":"Available recipes:\n    check          # The fast inner loop: skips the docs mega-test, the suite's ~137s long pole. Gate on `just test`.\n    checks         # The repo's mechanical checks, the same surface the Stop hook runs.\n    clippy         # Run clippy with the repo's lint set, the same surface the Stop hook checks.\n    default        # List available recipes.\n    drive          # The autonomous drive loop: a tick every 600s, live colorized output, Ctrl-C to stop. Run ONE.\n    euler-data DIR # `just test`. DIR holds your own copies of the raw data texts; fails loudly, never skips.\n    fmt            # Formatter check over every .toy file from the repo root down (exit 1 on drift).\n    fmt-write      # Rewrite drifted files in place (same exit code as the check).\n    peek           # Watch the current coordinator tick live (detaches with Ctrl-C, tick untouched).\n    test           # The final gate: the full test suite. Landing requires this green.\n    tick           # Fire one coordinator tick right now (zero tokens if there is nothing to do).\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"just --list","time":{"start":1788120585666,"end":1788120585667}},"id":"prt_0544ad528001nYugkc6RwngsHu","sessionID":"ses_fabb535ccffe1uMPqoZsBbW0jp","messageID":"msg_0544acb22001oehmQ51iNFYeKP"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788120586448,"sessionID":"ses_fabb535ccffe1uMPqoZsBbW0jp","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"chatcmpl-tool-94d1c92f3c76906a","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"gh issue view 149"},"output":"title:\tImplement Float (IEEE binary64 per ADR 0007) across the backends\nstate:\tOPEN\nauthor:\tkantord (Dániel Kántor)\nlabels:\t\ncomments:\t0\nassignees:\t\nprojects:\t\nmilestone:\t\nissue-type:\t\nparent:\t\nsub-issues:\t\nsub-issues-completed:\t\nblocked-by:\t\nblocking:\t\nnumber:\t149\n--\nBuild the Float type end to end, per docs/adr/0007-float-is-javascripts-double.md: IEEE 754\nbinary64, matching JavaScript's number representation, no alternative width, no decimal type.\n\nSemantics per gh:145 (the Q37 ruling): admit NaN/Infinity, division by zero returns Infinity\n(IEEE), matching IEEE 754. Division is a total function on Float; Int and Float division have\ndifferent failure behavior (Int still raises on zero divisor).\n\nNot yet settled, needs a call during implementation: exact float literal printing so all seven\nbackends agree byte for byte (default float formatting differs across languages) -- pick a\nformat and hold every backend to it. See draft.md Q37 in plans/questions.md for the fuller\nquestion shape if it still exists, otherwise use the ADR and gh:145 as the source of truth.\n\nAcceptance:\n- Float literals parse and type-check\n- arithmetic (+ - * /) and comparisons work across all seven backends with agreeing output\n- NaN/Infinity are producible and print identically across backends\n- division by zero on Float returns Infinity, not an error (contrast with Int)\n- corpus test coverage added for the above\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n","metadata":{"output":"title:\tImplement Float (IEEE binary64 per ADR 0007) across the backends\nstate:\tOPEN\nauthor:\tkantord (Dániel Kántor)\nlabels:\t\ncomments:\t0\nassignees:\t\nprojects:\t\nmilestone:\t\nissue-type:\t\nparent:\t\nsub-issues:\t\nsub-issues-completed:\t\nblocked-by:\t\nblocking:\t\nnumber:\t149\n--\nBuild the Float type end to end, per docs/adr/0007-float-is-javascripts-double.md: IEEE 754\nbinary64, matching JavaScript's number representation, no alternative width, no decimal type.\n\nSemantics per gh:145 (the Q37 ruling): admit NaN/Infinity, division by zero returns Infinity\n(IEEE), matching IEEE 754. Division is a total function on Float; Int and Float division have\ndifferent failure behavior (Int still raises on zero divisor).\n\nNot yet settled, needs a call during implementation: exact float literal printing so all seven\nbackends agree byte for byte (default float formatting differs across languages) -- pick a\nformat and hold every backend to it. See draft.md Q37 in plans/questions.md for the fuller\nquestion shape if it still exists, otherwise use the ADR and gh:145 as the source of truth.\n\nAcceptance:\n- Float literals parse and type-check\n- arithmetic (+ - * /) and comparisons work across all seven backends with agreeing output\n- NaN/Infinity are producible and print identically across backends\n- division by zero on Float returns Infinity, not an error (contrast with Int)\n- corpus test coverage added for the above\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"gh issue view 149","time":{"start":1788120586441,"end":1788120586444}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Let me start by reading the key context: AGENTS.md (already provided in system prompt, but let me verify), the issue, the ADR, and the previous issue 145. Let me get oriented in the worktree first.\n\nLet me start by looking at the repo structure and reading the issue.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_0544ad3a5001Q1GcHoAATupHi6","sessionID":"ses_fabb535ccffe1uMPqoZsBbW0jp","messageID":"msg_0544acb22001oehmQ51iNFYeKP"}}
